ype":"command_run","materiality_hint":{"possible_code_effect":true},"target":{"command":"cd /home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('finite_spectral_shadows.tex').read()\nold=\"\"\"\\\\begin{openproblem}[One-condition degeneracy cost]\\\\label{op:onecond}\nUnder the terminal-window filtration, conditionally on the nominal shell\nand on $h\\\\ge r-1$, the next leading coefficient vanishes with probability\nat most $\\\\tfrac13(1+\\\\epsilon_r)$, $\\\\sum\\\\epsilon_r<\\\\infty$, cellwise in\n$a$; hence $\\\\Pr[h\\\\ge r\\\\mid d_{\\\\mathrm{nom}}]\\\\le C_2\\\\,3^{-r}$. This is\nthe class-IV analogue of the class-bijectivity step in the proof of\n\\\\cref{op:flat} (measured: $0.13,\\\\,0.30,\\\\,0.33$ per level, uniform over\nshells), and it is the \\\\emph{only} remaining finite-side estimate.\n\\\\end{openproblem}\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"\\\\begin{theorem}[One-condition degeneracy cost; level-cost law]\n\\\\label{op:onecond}\nFix a unit $a$, a word $w$, and $d\\\\ge2$. Then, uniformly over $(w,a)$,\n\\\\[\n\\\\Pr_{w'}\\\\bigl[d_{\\\\mathrm{nom}}\\\\ge d\\\\ \\\\wedge\\\\ h(a)\\\\ge r\\\\bigr]\n\\;\\\\le\\;C_0\\\\,2^{-(d-3)}\\\\cdot\\\\frac23\\\\Bigl(\\\\frac47\\\\Bigr)^{r-1},\n\\\\]\nwith $C_0<1.355$ the pinning constant of \\\\cref{lem:pinning}. The\nlevel-cost constant is $\\\\lambda=\\\\frac47=0.5714\\\\ldots<3^{-1/2}$.\n\\\\end{theorem}\n\n\\\\begin{proof}\nReveal $w'$ forward and let $\\\\mathcal G_t=\\\\sigma(b_1',\\\\dots,b_t')$. The\nscale-$t$ digit of $\\\\mathcal L(a)$ requires $\\\\Delta C_i$ modulo\n$3^{\\\\,t-i+1}$ for $i\\\\le t$ only, so it is settled at time $t-1$, and the\nfreshest variable $\\\\beta:=b'_{t-1}$ enters solely through\n$C'_t=3C'_{t-1}+2^{B'_{t-2}}2^{\\\\beta}$.\n\n\\\\emph{(i) Support two; trichotomy.} At scale $t$ itself,\n$2^{\\\\beta}\\\\bmod3=(-1)^{\\\\beta}$, so\n$\\\\mathrm{digit}_t=W_t+\\\\kappa_t(-1)^{\\\\beta}$ with $W_t$ predictable and\n$\\\\kappa_t=\\\\pm2^{B'_{t-2}}u_t(a)$ a predictable unit. Hence\n$\\\\Pr[\\\\mathrm{digit}_t=0\\\\mid\\\\text{past}]\\\\in\\\\{0,\\\\tfrac13,\\\\tfrac23\\\\}$\naccording as $W_t\\\\equiv0,-\\\\kappa_t,+\\\\kappa_t$; in particular $\\\\le\\\\frac23$.\n\n\\\\emph{(ii) Three-value spread at the next scale.} At scale $t+1$ the same\n$\\\\beta$ enters through $2^{\\\\beta}\\\\bmod9$. Within a parity class the orbit\ntriple is $\\\\{2,8,5\\\\}$ (odd) or $\\\\{1,4,7\\\\}$ (even): \\\\emph{distinct\nmodulo $9$, congruent modulo $3$}. Hence, conditional on the parity class\nselected at scale $t$ and on \\\\emph{any} realization of all other\nvariables, the three mod-$6$ refinement classes $j$ of $\\\\beta$ shift the\nscale-$(t{+}1)$ base $W_{t+1}$ by three distinct second digits\n($3\\\\cdot\\\\{0,1,2\\\\}\\\\cdot$unit), so $W_{t+1}(j)$ runs over \\\\emph{all three}\nresidues bijectively, and by (i) the associated costs are a permutation of\n$(0,\\\\tfrac13,\\\\tfrac23)$. The within-class masses of $j$ are geometric,\nexactly $(\\\\tfrac{16}{21},\\\\tfrac4{21},\\\\tfrac1{21})$ for both parities, so\n\\\\[\n\\\\Pr[\\\\mathrm{digit}_{t+1}=0\\\\mid\\\\text{class, past}]\n\\\\le\\\\frac{16}{21}\\\\cdot\\\\frac23+\\\\frac4{21}\\\\cdot\\\\frac13+\\\\frac1{21}\\\\cdot0\n=\\\\frac47 .\n\\\\]\n\n\\\\emph{(iii) Chain.} The lift $h(a)\\\\ge r$ requires\n$\\\\mathrm{digit}_t=0$ for $t=d,\\\\dots,d+r-1$; the first scale pays\n$\\\\le\\\\frac23$ by (i) and each subsequent scale pays $\\\\le\\\\frac47$ by (ii)\n(each $\\\\beta$ serves once as fresh parity and once as refinement;\nconditioning on more and bounding uniformly is legitimate). \n\n\\\\emph{(iv) Shell factorization.} The depth-$d$ cascade\n$d_{\\\\mathrm{nom}}\\\\ge d$ is equivalent to congruences on the pairs\n$j\\\\le d-2$ (\\\\cref{thm:cascade} at depth $d$), disjoint from the peeling\nvariables $b'_j$, $j\\\\ge d-1$; the fixed-$w$ sequential pinning\n(\\\\cref{lem:pinning} at depth $d$) gives $C_0\\\\,2^{-(d-3)}$, and the\nuniform conditional bounds (i)--(iii) multiply against it.\n\\\\end{proof}\n\n\\\\begin{remark}\nThe trichotomy in (i) is exactly the measured structure ($\\\\Pr[h\\\\ge1]$\nper shell $\\\\approx0.13$, conditionals $0.30$--$0.33$), and the bound is\nhonest under adversarial conditioning: at $w=1^c$ (the heavy word) with\n$a=1$ the measured conditional level costs rise to\n$0.380,\\\\,0.429,\\\\,0.444$---approaching, but respecting, $4/7$. The\ninequality $\\\\frac47<3^{-1/2}$ is what the assembly requires:\n$\\\\sqrt3\\\\cdot\\\\frac47=0.9897<1$.\n\\\\end{remark}\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold2=\"\"\"\\\\begin{theorem}[Finite H23a, conditional on \\\\cref{op:onecond}]\n\\\\label{thm:final}\nGranted \\\\cref{op:onecond}, the class-IV row budget satisfies\n\\\\[\nR_{\\\\mathrm{IV}}(\\\\xi)\n\\\\le\\\\varphi\\\\,\\\\mu(x)\\\\sum_{d\\\\le c-2}K3^{-(d-2)}\\\\cdot C_23^{-(c-1-d)}\n\\\\le\\\\mathrm{poly}(c)\\\\,3^{-c/2},\n\\\\]\n(using the cellwise coset dichotomy to cap $|S|$ by the degenerate-cell\nmeasure, and $\\\\mu\\\\le\\\\sqrt{\\\\operatorname{Col}_c(c)}$ from \\\\cref{op:flat}),\nwhich is far subordinate to the cascade sector.\"\"\"\nnew2=\"\"\"\\\\begin{openproblem}[Cellwise summation]\\\\label{op:cellsum}\nFor class-IV pairs, $|S(w,w')|\\\\le C\\\\,\\\\#\\\\{a:\\\\,d_{\\\\mathrm{true}}(a)\\\\ge\nc-1\\\\}$ up to deep-cell contributions controlled by quadratic\n(Postnikov/Gauss) sums---the harmonic-analysis step in the regime of the\nproved \\\\cref{lem:vanish,lem:coset}; for cells in the linear regime\n($\\\\nu\\\\le(c+d)/2$) this follows from \\\\cref{lem:vanish} directly. This is\nthe sole remaining technical step.\n\\\\end{openproblem}\n\n\\\\begin{theorem}[Finite H23a, conditional on \\\\cref{op:cellsum}]\n\\\\label{thm:final}\nGranted \\\\cref{op:cellsum}, the class-IV row budget satisfies, by\n\\\\cref{op:onecond} (now a theorem) and Fubini over the degenerate cells,\n\\\\[\nR_{\\\\mathrm{IV}}(\\\\xi)\n\\\\le\\\\varphi\\\\,\\\\mu(x)\\\\,\\\\sup_w\\\\sum_{d\\\\le c-2}C_0 2^{-(d-3)}\\\\cdot\n\\\\tfrac23\\\\bigl(\\\\tfrac47\\\\bigr)^{c-2-d}\n\\\\le\\\\mathrm{poly}(c)\\\\,\\\\mu(x)\\\\,3^{c}\\\\bigl(\\\\tfrac47\\\\bigr)^{c}\n\\\\le\\\\mathrm{poly}(c)\\\\bigl(\\\\sqrt3\\\\cdot\\\\tfrac47\\\\bigr)^{c},\n\\\\]\nwith $\\\\sqrt3\\\\cdot\\\\frac47=0.9897<1$ (the $d$-sum is dominated by small\nshells since $\\\\frac12<\\\\frac47$),\"\"\"\nassert old2 in s\ns=s.replace(old2,new2)\nopen('finite_spectral_shadows.tex','w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode finite_spectral_shadows.tex >/tmp/fss.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode finite_spectral_shadows.tex >/tmp/fss.log 2>&1\ngrep -E \"^!\" /tmp/fss.log | head -3; pdfinfo finite_spectral_shadows.pdf | grep Pages","input_hash":"sha256:6b8bd6054620faa8948fc2e9137b4329c0b1ecd4be041e46b3d4ab6f64b23431","output_hash":"sha256:518a8e8111d28bbad8f9af3ef24ad4f298d2a6b37101805561750f46e20e3ab8","tool":"Bash"},"time":"2026-06-10T07:41:57Z"},{"actor":{"kind":"ai_tool","tool":"Claude Code"},"event_type":"command_run","materiality_hint":{"possible_code_effect":true},"target":{"command":"cd /home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory\ngrep -n \"conditional only on\\|op:onecond\\|op:cellsum\" finite_spectral_shadows.tex | grep -v \"^2[01]\" | head -12","input_hash":"sha256:1ab8cbfe655d22aea1ab144c34879f9ec7c0a486dac37e7e4d248fb813ee0340","output_hash":"sha256:b9dcff902bdbf238b475c96c7b2be09642aaad4c6d07315a64972f4e2c51c5ba","tool":"Bash"},"time":"2026-06-10T07:42:07Z"},{"actor":{"kind":"ai_tool","tool":"Claude Code"},"event_type":"command_run","materiality_hint":{"possible_code_effect":true},"target":{"command":"cd /home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory\nsed -n '2215,2222p' finite_spectral_shadows.tex; echo ----; sed -n '2588,2602p' finite_spectral_shadows.tex; echo ----\ngrep -n \"conditional only on\" finite_spectral_shadows.tex","input_hash":"sha256:039dac2276f313b727c02b73cfb495cc7c23473cb8ae28f0022da82346bfa319","output_hash":"sha256:ad92bd1b28de9d3dc9ddd1f4